---
import PageLayout from "../../layouts/PageLayout.astro";
import releases from "../../data/releases.json";
---
<PageLayout
  title="Release Notes & Version History — TotalRecalls"
  description="Complete release notes and version history for TotalRecalls Downloader and Smart Search Engine. What's new in each Windows release."
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: "Release Notes" }]}
>
  <h1>Release Notes</h1>

  <p class="lead">
    TotalRecalls is distributed as both a certified Microsoft Store application and a standalone portable Windows package.
    Every release is signed, verified, and self-contained on your local hardware.
  </p>

  <section>
    <h2>Current Production Release: {releases.releases[0].tag} ({releases.releases[0].date})</h2>
    <p class="text-muted-foreground">{releases.releases[0].title} — {releases.releases[0].summary}</p>
    <ul>
      {releases.releases[0].changes.map((c) => <li>{c}</li>)}
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Architecture &amp; Platform Security</h2>
    <p>
      TotalRecalls runs on 64-bit Windows 10 and Windows 11. Certified and distributed through the Microsoft Store,
      the application installs cleanly with one click, creates no background Windows services, and does not register
      system drivers. All network traffic is restricted strictly to the AI providers you explicitly connect to and
      the one-time Paddle license verification endpoint.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Update and Upgrade Policy</h2>
    <p>
      We maintain a clear distinction between maintenance updates and feature upgrades:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Maintenance Updates (Free for Life):</strong> Bug fixes, provider API adapter adjustments,
        and security patches for Downloader Pro are free for the lifetime of the product. When an AI provider
        adjusts their web session layout, updated adapters are delivered automatically via the Microsoft Store.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Feature Upgrades &amp; Add-Ons:</strong> Major architectural modules — such as the Smart Search
        Engine (SSE) semantic vector add-on, future local RAG containers, and multi-device memory sync — are
        engineered as standalone optional utilities that enhance your local library without recurring subscriptions.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Release Artifacts Summary</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Microsoft Store Edition:</strong> Package family <code>34690AndreG.TotalRecalls</code> — automatic silent updates, sandbox isolation.</li>
      <li><strong>Smart Search Engine Add-On:</strong> <code>TotalRecalls-Smart-Search-Engine-1.0.0.zip</code> (0.78 MB) — offline self-contained search UI bundle with PDF &amp; Markdown user guides.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</PageLayout>
